WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
Hey, this is  Presh Talwalkar

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.680
A version of this problem was used as an Amazon interview question

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:15.440
A cable of 80 meters is hanging from the top of two poles that are both 50 meters from the ground

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:23.120
What is the distance between the two poles to one decimal place if the center of the cable is

00:00:23.859 --> 00:00:28.169
(a) 20 meters above the ground and (b) 10 meters above the ground

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:35.380
Now to be more specific a version of problem B was asked during an Amazon interview

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.460
But I've included problem A because it's interesting mathematically

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.100
Can you figure it out?

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:47.789
Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for a solution

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.870
So, let's solve the case of 20 meters above the ground

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:12.499
We have the ground. We have two poles of 50 meters each and we have a hanging cable. That's 80 meters long the

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:19.789
Center of this cable is 20 meters from the ground and we want to solve for the distance between the two poles

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:26.479
Now I'll admit I had forgotten how to solve this kind of problem. So I had to look up some formulas online

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:33.139
Many of the websites referred to the physics interpretation which involved weights and tensions

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:36.290
And I just wanted to get to some of the mathematical formulas

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.750
So I found a great reference

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:44.239
from Neil Chatterjee and Bogdan G. Nita., "The hanging cable problem for practical

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:51.739
applications" in the Atlantic Electronic Journal of Mathematics. I provided a link in the video description and I recommend you check it out

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.619
So we'll solve this problem using symmetry and a convenient coordinate system

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:02.449
First we'll split up the cable into two lengths of 40

00:02:03.539 --> 00:02:07.759
Next we'll consider only the distance from the center of the cable to one of the poles

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:11.539
We can then double that distance to get the distance between the two poles

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:19.189
We'll also use a convenient coordinate system that's centered at the center of this hanging cable in

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.959
Other words the y-axis goes at the center of the cable and the x-axis

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:28.429
Also goes so that it's just touching and tangent to the center of the cable

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:32.090
so we want to calculate this distance x

00:02:32.849 --> 00:02:40.099
From the paper, the general catenary equation that's tangent to the ground or the x-axis takes the following form

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:46.560
y is equal to a cosh of the quantity x over a minus a

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:53.840
Furthermore the top of the pole in this diagram will be at the coordinate x, 30

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:57.890
So

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:02.899
We can use the point at the top of the pole to get one equation

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:09.110
this simplifies to be a cosh of x over a is equal to 30 plus a

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:16.720
It'll be convenient to divide both sides by a so a the cosh of x over a is equal to 30 plus a all over a

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.560
Now we have another equation which is using the length of half of the cable

00:03:23.829 --> 00:03:29.789
This equation will be a times the sinh of x over a is equal to the length of 40 meters

00:03:30.519 --> 00:03:35.759
we'll again divide both sides by a to get the sinh of x over a is equal to 40 over a

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:40.200
Now we can use the hyperbolic identity

00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:48.539
That the cosh squared of t minus the sinh squared of t is equal to 1 so we substitute in the values

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:53.429
We've just arrived and we can solve for this value of a as a quadratic equation

00:03:54.129 --> 00:03:57.388
We get that a is equal to 35 over 3

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:05.939
We now figure out this unknown parameter and we can then use it in our second equation with sinh to

00:04:06.189 --> 00:04:12.959
Solve for the value of x and we end up that X is approximately equal to 22.7 meters

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:19.019
Which we will then double to get the distance between the two poles as 45.4 meters

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:24.749
Amazing. So now how do we solve the next problem?

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:29.459
What if the cable is only hanging 10 meters above the ground

00:04:30.729 --> 00:04:34.619
now suppose you try and go through the same exact method

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:39.030
At this point the top of the pole will be at a point x, 40

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:47.250
So we'll use the same equations and we'll substitute in the new values from this particular case

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:50.759
Now when you substitute it into the hyperbolic identity

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:56.900
You get the following equation and if you try to solve it you run into a problem

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:00.340
This equation has no solution

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.780
So what is going on?

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:08.500
Well, we're gonna need to think about this problem logically

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:15.940
The hanging cable is supposed to be 10 meters off the ground, which is 40 meters from the top of the pole

00:05:19.539 --> 00:05:26.908
But half of the cable is already 40 meters in other words the cable must be folded exactly in half and

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:32.639
That means the two pole are coincident. There are zero meters apart

00:05:34.509 --> 00:05:40.558
So our diagram is actually going to look like the following. We don't actually have a hanging cable between

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:45.299
Two poles we actually have this cable is going directly down

00:05:45.669 --> 00:05:49.288
From the two poles because they are exactly at the same spot

00:05:50.289 --> 00:05:52.289
no equations required

00:05:53.139 --> 00:05:58.918
many employees can mindlessly calculate the answer, but how many will think before they calculate and

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:03.990
To be honest, I completely missed this problem because I didn't see the trick

00:06:04.749 --> 00:06:09.359
but I'd like to make videos about these problems because it's like the old saying goes

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:15.160
Fool me once shame on you fool me twice...You can't get fooled again

